# Feature delivery

Build one milestone at a time, in the order in the root `AGENTS.md`. A milestone is one demoable slice, not a whole layer of the system.

When a feature is finished and its tests pass:

1. Add `doc/features/<feature-slug>/AGENTS.md` describing what was built, which PRD and RFC sections it covers, how to run its tests, and what is still open.
2. Commit only that feature. The message names the feature. Do not mention Cursor, the editor, or the agent in the commit message.
3. Push that commit to the configured remote.

Do not batch unrelated features into one commit. Do not push secrets. Leave the next milestone unstarted until the current one is pushed.
